<object id="Diagnosis" label="Diagnosis" tooltip="A shared conceptual abstraction for onsite and online diagnostic records. Findings include assessment, treatment, laboratory-result entries, notes, attachments and follow-up information where the corresponding workflow supports them. The veterinarian can retain/add consent during diagnosis; moving initial consent to admin examination does not remove that capability. Finalization synchronizes nonempty prescription content to the patient&apos;s plan. Automatic prescription printing runs only when printable medicine rows exist. sourceType and sourceId distinguish onsite and online records, so this overview does not imply that their tables share an identifier namespace or a declared inheritance hierarchy.
Supporting mappings: vet_diagnoses, online_consultation_diagnoses"><mxCell style="swimlane;html=0;horizontal=1;startSize=30;align=center;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#111111;fillColor=#ffffff;swimlaneFillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#111111;strokeWidth=1.2;rounded=0;collapsible=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1096" y="691" width="198" height="222" as="geometry"/></mxCell></object>
